<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- Fix14: Alien | Rimworld (niz.xenomorphtype) ships its Dubs Bad Hygiene compatibility defs in
       an UNVERSIONED folder - Compatibility/DubsBadHygiene/Defs/DBHInfiltrationNetwork.xml:18 - so
       they load unconditionally, and XMT_DBHInfiltrationList lists <li>WaterTrough</li>.
       DBH IS active and DOES define WaterTrough (836308268/1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Buildings/
       BuildingsB_Hygiene.xml:251), but tags it DBHThirst="true" - DBH's own conditional-def
       attribute - and DBH drops those defs when its thirst module is off, leaving the reference
       dangling -> "Could not resolve cross-reference to Verse.ThingDef named WaterTrough".
       FIRST ATTEMPT (failed, don't retry): PatchOperationConditional on
       /Defs/ThingDef[defName="WaterTrough"] with a <nomatch> removal. Verified against a real run -
       the error survived. DBH strips DBHThirst defs AFTER the XML patch phase, so at patch time the
       def is still present and the conditional never fires. No XML-time test can see the strip.
       So: remove the reference unconditionally.
       BROKEN BY AN UPSTREAM UPDATE, 2026-08-05: the original xpath was /Defs//things/li[...], which
       was correct when written - the 2026-08-03 log shows zero WaterTrough errors. Alien|Rimworld
       rewrote this file on 2026-08-05 17:25 and the reference now lives under <endpointDefs>, so
       the xpath stopped matching and the error came back. success=Always meant the breakage was
       completely silent for four days; nothing in the log said the patch had gone dead.
       The xpath below is therefore scoped to the DEF rather than to a field name: any descendant
       <li> of XMT_DBHInfiltrationList. That still cannot touch another mod's lists, but it survives
       the field being renamed again, which is exactly how this broke.
       TRADEOFF: if you ever switch DBH's thirst module ON, WaterTrough will exist and this patch
       will still strip it from the infiltration network - xenomorphs won't treat troughs as a water
       source. That is the only behavioural cost. If you enable thirst, delete this file.
       success=Always so it stays silent if Alien|Rimworld ever drops the reference itself. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove">
    <success>Always</success>
    <xpath>/Defs/Xenomorphtype.InfiltrationNetworkDef[defName="XMT_DBHInfiltrationList"]//li[text()="WaterTrough"]</xpath>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
